============================================================
λ-ENGINE  ·  Cantor monad × Gödel comonad
g := Cantor ∘ Gödel  (PRIMITIVE_THEOREMS §81)
============================================================

── Cantor power-set monad P ──────────────────────────────
  m = P{'α', 'β', 'γ'}
  η('α') = P{'α'}

  Powerset of {a,b,c}:
    ∅
    {'a'}
    {'b'}
    {'c'}
    {'a', 'b'}
    {'c', 'a'}
    {'c', 'b'}
    {'c', 'a', 'b'}

  Cantor diagonal witness on 3 sets:
    enum = [P{0, 2}, P{1}, P{0, 1, 2}]
    D    = P{}  (differs from each S_i at index i)
    i=0: 0 ∈ S_0, 0 ∉ D  → differ: True
    i=1: 1 ∈ S_1, 1 ∉ D  → differ: True
    i=2: 2 ∈ S_2, 2 ∉ D  → differ: True

  Monad laws: {'left_unit': '✓', 'right_unit': '✓', 'associativity': '✓'}

── Gödel encoding comonad G ──────────────────────────────
  G('α')         = G('α', #1)
  ε(G('α'))      = 'α'
  δ(G('α'))      = G(G('α', #1), #1)
  δ(δ(G('α')))   = G(G(G('α', #1), #1), #1)

  Gödel sentence (PA): G('Sentence #2 is not provable in PA.', #2)

  Fano plane (octonionic δ — co-type octonions, d=0):
    δ(e_1) = G((2, 4), #3)
    δ(e_2) = G((3, 5), #4)
    δ(e_3) = G((4, 6), #5)
    δ(e_4) = G((5, 7), #6)
    δ(e_5) = G((6, 1), #7)
    δ(e_6) = G((7, 2), #8)
    δ(e_7) = G((1, 3), #9)

  Comonad laws: {'counit_left': '✓', 'counit_right': '✓', 'coassociativity': '✓'}

── Distributive law λ: P(G) → G(P) ───────────────────────
  Input  P(G(T)) = P{G('α', #1), G('β', #10), G('γ', #11)}
  Output G(P(T)) = G(P{'α', 'β', 'γ'}, #{1,10,11})
  Decoded P(T)   = P{'α', 'β', 'γ'}

── Frobenius condition μ∘δ=id ────────────────────────────
  frobenius_check(G('α')) = True  ← True: λ planted

Frobenius μ∘δ=id requires BOTH μ (monad) AND δ (comonad).
  monad_cantor  has μ  but no δ  → cannot test
  comonad_goedel has δ  but no μ  → cannot test
  lam() plants both simultaneously → Frobenius holds
  d(monad⊗comonad, λ) = 2.2361   → gap is non-zero
  λ must be planted, not assembled.  (PRIMITIVE_THEOREMS §23/§81)

